.TH RTGO 1 "September 2026" "unix-core" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rtgo \- Root Go: fast passwordless privilege executor restricted to wheel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rtgo
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rtgo
is a fast, minimalist, POSIX-compliant privilege elevation utility that executes commands directly as root without prompting for a password. Execution is strictly restricted to members of the
.B wheel
administrative group (or root).
.PP
When invoked,
.B rtgo
validates that the caller belongs to the
.B wheel
group, cleanses dangerous environment variables, drops supplementary groups, assumes root credentials, and executes the specified command via
.BR execvp (3).
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Group Restriction:
The binary permissions must be set to \fIchmod 4750\fR owned by \fIroot:wheel\fR. In addition, an internal runtime verification ensures only members of group \fIwheel\fR can execute it.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Environment Sanitization:
Dangerous variables such as \fBLD_PRELOAD\fR, \fBLD_LIBRARY_PATH\fR, and \fBIFS\fR are stripped, and a secure \fBPATH\fR is enforced if unset.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Zero External Dependencies:
Unlike tools requiring PAM or crypt, \fBrtgo\fR has zero cryptographic or dynamic authentication overhead, minimizing attack surface.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion of the executed command.
.TP
.B 1
Access denied (not in wheel), SUID bit missing, or invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rtdo (1),
.BR doas (1),
.BR sudo (8)
